-- title:
--   Transpose of U_q preserves the two-cusp rational set
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a nonzero natural number with $p \mid M$ and $p^2 \nmid M$, and let $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ be a subgroup containing every unit $u$ whose image under the reduction `ZMod.unitsMap` along $M/p \mid M$ is $1$. Let $q$ be a prime dividing $M$ with $q \neq p$. Write $\Gamma_H(M)$ for the subgroup [`CohCarrier.GammaH M H`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) of $\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$, the image in $\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$ of the preimage of $H$ under the character $\Gamma_0(M) \to (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ given by the lower-right entry. Let $f$ be a weight-two cusp form on $\Gamma_H(M)$ lying in [`CuspForm.twoCuspIntegralSet M H 2 p (algebraMap ℚ ℂ).range`](def/CuspForm_TwoCuspLattice.html#L54), i.e. such that for every $t$ in the subring `heckeRingH M H 2` of $\mathbb{C}$-linear endomorphisms of weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_H(M)$ generated by the range of `heckeGenH` (with parameter $\emptyset$), every Atkin–Lehner datum $W$ for $(M,p)$ (a factorisation $M = pR$ together with $a,b \in \mathbb{Z}$ satisfying $pa - Rb = 1$) and every $n$, the $n$-th $q$-expansion coefficients of $t f$ and of $(t f)\mid_2 W$ are both rational. Let $Y$ be a weight-two cusp form on $\Gamma_H(M)$ whose underlying function is $\sum_{j<q} f \mid_2 \bigl(\mathrm{diag}(q,1)\,{}^{t}T^{Mj}\bigr) = \sum_{j<q} f \mid_2 \begin{pmatrix} q & 0 \\ Mj & 1\end{pmatrix}$. Then $Y$ also lies in [`CuspForm.twoCuspIntegralSet M H 2 p (algebraMap ℚ ℂ).range`](def/CuspForm_TwoCuspLattice.html#L54).
--
--   The operator $f \mapsto \sum_{j<q} f\mid_2\begin{pmatrix} q&0\\Mj&1\end{pmatrix}$ is the transpose of the Hecke operator $U_q$ at a prime $q$ dividing the level; the statement says that it preserves the property of having rational $q$-expansions at both the cusp $\infty$ and the Atkin–Lehner translate of it, after applying any operator of the Hecke ring. It is used by [`CuspForm.exists_not_dvd_and_coe_eq_smul_sum_slash_transpose_and_heckeU_eq_of_mem_twoCuspIntegralSet`](thm.html#CuspForm.exists_not_dvd_and_coe_eq_smul_sum_slash_transpose_and_heckeU_eq_of_mem_twoCuspIntegralSet) in the construction of suitable rational cusp forms at level $M$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CuspForm_mem_twoCuspIntegralSet_range_of_coe_eq_sum_slash_transpose_of_mem_twoCuspIntegralSet_range.lean

import Mathlib
